%description:
StochasticErrorModel: symbolErrorRate only, APSK bit-level transmitter.

symbolErrorRate = 1e-4. The transmitter is the layered (bit level) one, so that the transmissions have a bit model; the receiver is the packet level ApskReceiver with the error model.
Two APSK hosts (CsmaCaInterface, ApskRadio, 100 Mbit/s, scalar) with the layered ApskLayeredTransmitter (level of detail "bit", 64-QAM, no forward error correction, so that the bit model has the 64 header and 8396 data bits of the MAC frame) and the ApskReceiver, 20 m apart, unicast UDP packets without MAC acknowledgements.
Each frame is received with probability 1 - PER = 0.8685, so that the number of packets the sink receives is binomial with mean 434.2 and standard deviation 7.6; the test requires it to be within 4 standard deviations of the mean, [405, 464] (a correct model misses that with probability of about 6e-5, and the run is deterministic).
The run must end without an error. The error rates that the sink's radio records from the ErrorRateInd tags, and the rates of the whole frame, of its header and of its data that the error model returns (recorded by the StochasticErrorModelProbe), must equal, to a relative precision of 1e-6, the values of the closure that the NED documentation of StochasticErrorModel gives (computed independently of the C++ code).

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib
*.*.wlan[*].radio.transmitter.typename = "ApskLayeredTransmitter"
*.*.wlan[*].radio.transmitter.levelOfDetail = "bit"
*.*.wlan[*].radio.transmitter.encoder.typename = "ApskEncoder"
*.*.wlan[*].radio.transmitter.modulator.typename = "ApskModulator"
*.*.wlan[*].radio.transmitter.modulator.modulation = "QAM-64"
**.fcsMode = "computed"
**.checksumMode = "computed"
**.radio.receiver.errorModel.symbolErrorRate = 0.0001
include ../../lib/stochastic-errormodel-apsk.ini

%postrun-command: awk -v lo=405 -v hi=464 -v rate="packetErrorRate=0.13151681153879691 bitErrorRate=1.6667361153577254e-05 symbolErrorRate=0.0001" -v want="bitErrorRate.DATA=1.6667361153577254e-05 bitErrorRate.HEADER=1.6667361153577254e-05 bitErrorRate.WHOLE=1.6667361153577254e-05 packetErrorRate.DATA=0.13058988885332168 packetErrorRate.HEADER=0.0010661512600224077 packetErrorRate.WHOLE=0.13151681153879691 symbolErrorRate.DATA=0.0001 symbolErrorRate.HEADER=0.0001 symbolErrorRate.WHOLE=0.0001" -f ../../lib/stochastic-errormodel.awk results/*.sca > verdict.out
%contains: verdict.out
verdict=PASS
%not-contains: test.out
<!> Error
